%% Sequence 1: happy path of one reading → campaign → queue → UI
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant OEM as OEM cloud (simulator)
  participant K as Kafka (Redpanda)
  participant N as Normaliser
  participant R as Redis
  participant SP as State processor
  participant PG as Postgres
  participant CE as Campaign engine
  participant WS as Workshop
  participant API as API
  participant UI as Web board
  OEM->>K: produce raw reading (raw.oem-a.v1, key = VIN)
  K->>N: consume batch
  N->>R: anti-replay check + sequence (Lua CAS per VIN)
  N->>K: produce canonical Avro (telemetry.canonical.v1)
  N->>K: commit raw offsets (after produce acks)
  K->>SP: consume canonical
  SP->>SP: deviation vs own normal − peers, EW trend, k of n
  SP->>PG: incident row + hourly telemetry (COPY)
  SP->>K: produce OPEN (incidents.v1)
  K->>CE: consume incident
  CE->>PG: tx: join (PK campaign, vin), Poisson guard → OPEN, clues, outbox row
  CE-->>K: outbox relay → campaign.events.v1 (OPENED)
  K->>WS: consume incident + campaign event
  WS->>PG: tx: re-rank depot, new queue version, outbox row
  WS-->>K: outbox relay → queue.events.v1
  K->>API: consume (SSE bus, tenant filter)
  API-->>UI: SSE "queue" (a change notice, no data)
  UI->>API: GET /depots/:id/queue (JWT)
  API->>PG: tx as cw_api: SET LOCAL tenant (RLS), read, audit + outbox
  API-->>UI: ranked queue with reasons and cost of waiting
